<Content title="Privacy Policy | OpenArabic" description="What OpenArabic collects, how it is used, and your rights." canonical="/privacy">
  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="quiet">Effective date: January 1, 2025. Last updated: November 1, 2026.</p>
    <p>This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and your rights.</p>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account information</h3>
    <p>When you create an account, we collect your email address. If you use Apple or Google Sign In, we receive basic profile information from those services.</p>
    <h3>Learning data</h3>
    <p>We store your reading progress, vocabulary lists, practice session history, review performance, and app preferences such as theme, audio settings and notifications.</p>
    <h3>Voice answers</h3>
    <p>Your voice is transcribed on your device and the audio is never uploaded. The text of your answer is saved.</p>
    <h3>Usage analytics</h3>
    <p>In the app, we use Mixpanel to record events like sign in, sign up, practice sessions and the title and category of the texts you open, linked to your account. On this website, and only if you agree, we use Google Analytics to see how visitors find and use it.</p>
    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <p>We use your data to provide the learning service, sync your progress across devices, personalize your learning, send practice reminders if you enable them, and improve the app.</p>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <h3>Supabase</h3>
    <p>We use Supabase for authentication, database and file storage.</p>
    <h3>Mixpanel</h3>
    <p>We use Mixpanel in the app to understand which features get used and to improve the learning experience. Its events are linked to your account. The app does not currently ask before sending them.</p>
    <h3>Meta (Facebook)</h3>
    <p>The app sends a small number of app events to Meta, so we can tell whether an ad was worth running: that the app was opened, an account was created, the intro was finished, or a practice session was completed, along with the technical details the Meta SDK attaches, such as device model and system version. On Android your device advertising ID is included. This applies whether or not you installed from an ad, and the app does not currently ask first. We do not send Meta your name, your email or what you study. We never ask to track you across other apps.</p>
    <h3 id="analytics">Google Analytics</h3>
    <p>Only if you agree on this website, we use Google Analytics to see how visitors find and use it, such as page views and referral sources. It sets cookies, and the data goes to Google. Because this site is about Islamic texts, visits could suggest your beliefs. If you refuse, or make no choice, nothing is loaded from Google and no analytics cookie is set. Your choice is stored in your browser, and it applies to this website, not the app. You can change it at any time on the <a href="/analytics-choice">analytics choice</a> page.</p>
    <h3>Sentry</h3>
    <p>We use Sentry for error tracking and crash reporting.</p>
    <h3>Apple and Google</h3>
    <p>If you sign in with Apple or Google, their privacy policies apply to the sign-in.</p>
    <h2>Data security</h2>
    <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections and secure authentication. No internet service is completely secure.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can access, update or delete your account data. To delete your account and its data, see <a href="/account-deletion">account deletion</a>.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>OpenArabic is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. We will tell you about significant changes through the app or by email.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Write to <a href="mailto:yunus@edenmind.com">yunus@edenmind.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Content>
